- Answer points to return:
  - SYSPROP is a SYSCTL register in Chapter 5 and is specifically framed by Dynamic Power Management plus its own register description.
  - FLASHPP and SSIZE are not SYSCTL registers on TM4C129; they are Chapter 8 Internal Memory registers.
  - Page numbers confirmed from the local extracted manual text: Device Identification page 233, Dynamic Power Management page 254, SYSPROP page 299, FLASHPP page 675, SSIZE page 677.
  - SYSPROP field summary: presence bits for FPU and several sleep or deep-sleep power-management capabilities.
  - FLASHPP field summary: flash feature and size reporting, including prefetch, mirror mode, DMA flash access, EEPROM sector size, flash sector size, and flash size.
  - SSIZE field summary: implemented SRAM size only.
  - Recommendation: for TM4C129 capability work, SYSPROP is a better next SYSCTL target than legacy DC0/DC1, and FLASHPP plus SSIZE are the better memory-capability targets even though they live in Internal Memory rather than SYSCTL.
